# Diagnostic codes

Every failure is a `*diag.Diag` that names what, where, why, and the fix. Do not
fix an error code from memory — read the lesson:

```
ultra explain DI0001      # the worked fix behind any code
ultra codes               # the whole registry, one line per code
```

The same text is available to agents via the `ultra mcp` `explain`/`codes` tools,
and in Go as `diag.Lesson(code)`. The generated index of every code lives in the
ultrastack module at `references/errors.md`.

Prefix → domain: `DI00xx` graph shape, `DI01xx` scopes & families, `DI02xx`
lifecycle, `UV00xx` static-analyzer lints.
